# m2_play: the preview GIF script. A on the title at 30, hold still and fire through the
# opening gnat strings (60-239), then sweep up 40 / hold 20 / down 40 / hold 20 to 3960.
# Since M5 there is no bomb; two short hold-B rewinds:
# - B 2084..2093 (10 frames = 20 ticks): game tick 2053 -> 2033, fuel 180 -> 160. The
#   inputs keep their update indices, so after the release the sweep runs 30 ticks ahead of
#   the world (10 frames not simulated + 20 ticks undone).
# - B 3320..3334 (15 frames = 30 ticks): game tick 3258 -> 3228, fuel 180 -> 150 (the
#   refill had topped it up again). Under the catch-up clock it fell in the stage-1 boss
#   fight; since the mode paces it is in stage 1's waves again.
# The press frame is already MANUAL (state 5); the release frame is PLAYING without a tick.
# Since M7 (Bullet hell for real) the sweep cannot live through stage 1 any more: in a normal
# game it spends its three rewinds and dies. So it plays in the endless probe mode
# (debug_probe at 31: a hit is counted in debug_hits and charges the power loss, a level and a
# fork, plus 80 mercy, at once; no rewind, the game goes on), and the old "survives with all
# three rewinds" pin becomes M7's acceptance bound for the sweep in stage 1: at least 6 hits
# (PLAN.md M7 "Difficulty targets"; 14 when re-pinned for the catch-up clock, 15 for the
# mode paces).
# Re-pinned for the mode paces (NORMAL: the table clock hurries, 3 ticks a tick, only on an
# empty field, and the fire ramp counts real stage ticks): the table runs slower than under
# the catch-up clock (floor 3, 4 ticks a tick), so every crate moved later and stage 1's
# table no longer ends inside the run (WARNING at 4110: phase 0 at the end, as before the
# catch-up; under it WARNING 2883, boss 3063). Crates on the way: F2 at 852, the hit at 870
# takes it back (F1, mercy 142), the cores crate at 1341, F2 again at 1653 (lost to the hit
# at 1716), fork 1 at 1866 (lost to the hit at 2136), the A crate at 2208 swaps F1 for A1
# (11), the retry shield at 2365 absorbs the hit at 2448 (shield 0, hits still 6). (Under
# the catch-up clock: F2 780, hit 1128, fork 1345, A 1619, shield 1650, absorbed at 1705.)
# Identity 0 on every frame from 31 when written.
--frames 4000 --call-at "31 debug_probe" --dump-exports debug_state,debug_score,debug_hits,debug_fuel,debug_grazes,debug_weapon,debug_forks,debug_phase --expect "debug_score > 570" --expect "debug_state == 1" --expect "debug_hits >= 6" --expect "debug_phase == 0" --at "851 debug_weapon == 1" --at "852 debug_weapon == 2" --at "869 debug_hits == 1" --at "870 debug_hits == 2" --at "870 debug_weapon == 1" --at "870 debug_mercy == 142" --at "1341 debug_cores == 1" --at "1866 debug_forks == 1" --at "2136 debug_forks == 0" --at "2207 debug_weapon == 1" --at "2208 debug_weapon == 11" --at "2365 debug_shield == 1" --at "2447 debug_shield == 1" --at "2448 debug_shield == 0" --at "2448 debug_hits == 6" --at "2083 debug_state == 1" --at "2084 debug_state == 5" --at "2093 debug_fuel == 160" --at "2094 debug_state == 1" --at "2094 debug_game_tick == 2033" --at "3999 debug_phase == 0" --at "3320 debug_state == 5" --at "3334 debug_game_tick == 3228" --at "3335 debug_state == 1" --at "3335 debug_fuel == 150" --at "1500 debug_history_check == 0" --at "2090 debug_history_check == 0" --at "3000 debug_history_check == 0" --at "3999 debug_history_check == 0"
